mysqlnd: the MySQL Native Driver, the client library of mysqli and
pdo_mysql in PHP itself (no libmysqlclient), with the compressed
protocol on the zlib of the base system, without OpenSSL: TLS to the
server through the module openssl when a site asks for it, no logins
caching_sha2_password (the default of MySQL 8 and later) and
sha256_password (MariaDB has neither); php82-mysqlnd-openssl has them. A
module of its own here (a part of the core in the official lang/php82).

The module mysqlnd of PHP 8.2 for php82 of azsupport/ports, which
installs side by side with the other versions of PHP:
lib/php/20220829/mysqlnd.so, loaded by its ini in etc/php82/conf.d, its
headers in include/php82/php/ext/mysqlnd.
